  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Inferir según el tiempo",
    "@en": "Inferir according to time"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**듯하다** presenta una inferencia: con adjetivos en presente se usa **-(으)ㄴ 듯하다** (피곤한 듯해요 = parece cansado); con verbos en presente, **-는 듯하다** (쉬는 듯해요 = parece que descansa); con verbos en futuro, **-(으)ㄹ 듯하다** (올 듯해요 = parece que vendrá). Con nombres: 학생인 듯해요 = parece estudiante.",
     "@en": "**듯하다** has an inference: with adjectives in present it is used **-(으)ㄴ 듯하다** (피곤한 듯해요 = seems tired); with verbs in present, **-는 듯하다** (쉬는 듯해요 = seems to rest); with verbs in future, **-(으)ㄹ 듯하다** (올 듯해요 = seems to be coming). With names: 학생인 듯해요 = looks like a student."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Matiz y registro",
    "@en": "Matiz and registration"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**-(으)ㄴ/는 듯하다** aparece mucho en explicaciones y textos cuidados; **-나 보다** es frecuente en inferencias conversacionales, mientras que **-(으)ㄹ 것 같다** sirve para muchas opiniones y predicciones. No son equivalencias exactas de «más seguro» o «más suave»: el matiz depende del contexto.",
     "@en": "**-(으)ㄴ/는 듯하다** appears a lot in careful explanations and texts; **-나 보다** is common in conversational inferences, while **-(으)ㄹ 것 같다** serves many opinions and predictions. They are not exact equivalencies of «safer» or «softer»: the nuance depends on the context."
    }
   ]
  },
